WEBVTT

00:02.200 --> 00:09.070
I have a feeling like fall mornings are
similar to summer evenings.

00:10.940 --> 00:15.000
When I'm enveloped in this light,

00:15.610 --> 00:19.380
memories of her spring up in my mind.

00:24.650 --> 00:27.620
Ichika, you're going to be late for school!

00:27.620 --> 00:28.720
Coming!

00:30.290 --> 00:35.960
Memories of that girl who disappeared
along with the summer...

00:46.430 --> 00:53.630
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

00:46.430 --> 00:53.630
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

00:53.650 --> 01:00.360
Setsunai hodo mune utsu kagirinai kibou

00:53.650 --> 01:00.360
This unbounded hope that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

01:01.160 --> 01:08.960
Hakanasa wo masu hibi wo
irodoru wa kisetsu no kaze

01:01.160 --> 01:08.960
The days pass by, becoming more fleeting,
colored by the season's wind

01:09.000 --> 01:13.670
Kioku no kakera ga sawagidashita yo

01:09.000 --> 01:13.670
The fragments of memory started running wild

01:14.270 --> 01:22.670
Arinomama wo mitomete
haruka tsumuida hikari ga

01:14.270 --> 01:22.670
One more time, I want to hold the
spindle of far off light close to my breast,

01:22.710 --> 01:30.340
Kieru mae ni mou ichido
kono mune ni dakishimete

01:22.710 --> 01:30.340
Before it disappears, before
I accept the way things are now

01:32.420 --> 01:39.620
Omoi wo ima hanadete hatenai asu ni kazasu yo

01:32.420 --> 01:39.620
I now play my feelings,
out to the endless tomorrow!

01:39.630 --> 01:46.770
Mirai wo egaku ao ni kono te wo nobashite

01:39.630 --> 01:46.770
Hold out this hand to the blue-painted future

01:46.940 --> 01:54.070
Kasokushiteku sekai yo douka
yasashii mama de ite

01:46.940 --> 01:54.070
The world accelerates, please let it stay this kind

01:54.180 --> 02:01.680
Setsunai hodo mune utsu afuredasu negai

01:54.180 --> 02:01.680
This overflowing wish that beats in my breast
to the point of melancholy

02:23.240 --> 02:24.230
Ichika...

02:29.650 --> 02:30.480
Ichika...

02:30.880 --> 02:34.250
How do you know my name?

02:34.650 --> 02:36.140
I'm sorry, Ichika.

02:36.750 --> 02:38.450
I really am sorry...

02:39.290 --> 02:40.450
Farewell...

02:40.990 --> 02:41.720
And...

02:42.020 --> 02:45.060
What do you mean? Who are you?

02:45.060 --> 02:46.830
What in the world do you...

02:46.830 --> 02:49.900
I am you, and you are me...

02:49.900 --> 02:52.160
But I...

03:09.080 --> 03:10.050
A dream?

03:12.050 --> 03:16.550
I had a dream the final day
of the first term of school,

03:16.660 --> 03:18.420
before summer break began.

03:18.790 --> 03:21.820
It was a fateful dream, and yet...

03:22.900 --> 03:26.060
I kind of feel like I had a dream...

03:30.200 --> 03:34.700
Early Summer's Encounter

03:36.340 --> 03:39.680
I am Ichika Tachibana, 14 years old.

03:39.680 --> 03:43.140
I go to Kamakura Girls Academy,
and am in my second year of middle school.

03:51.990 --> 03:53.360
Good morning!

03:53.660 --> 03:55.400
Good morning, Ichika dear.

03:55.400 --> 03:56.430
Good morning.

03:56.430 --> 03:59.330
This is my mother and father.

03:59.740 --> 04:01.640
My father works for a construction company.

04:02.500 --> 04:05.770
My mother does flower arranging.

04:11.050 --> 04:12.950
Is something the matter, Ichika dear?

04:12.950 --> 04:17.390
Oh, I apologize, Mother. I had an odd dream.

04:17.390 --> 04:19.350
A dream? What kind of dream?

04:19.350 --> 04:23.290
Well, I'm pretty sure I had a dream, but...

04:23.290 --> 04:25.020
I can't remember it!

04:26.660 --> 04:29.060
Finished already? You need to eat properly.

04:29.060 --> 04:31.930
It's time for me to go. Thank you for the meal.

04:32.230 --> 04:34.770
Look at that, you're right. Hurry up, Ichika dear!

04:34.770 --> 04:37.140
Can't be late for the end of term ceremony.

04:37.140 --> 04:39.130
Right! See you later!

04:41.610 --> 04:45.100
This is like the final day for her, I guess...

04:45.850 --> 04:46.710
Yes...

04:59.560 --> 05:01.390
Sei, Kail

05:03.570 --> 05:05.470
Ichika, good morning.

05:05.470 --> 05:07.400
Summer vacation starts tomorrow, yes?

05:07.400 --> 05:10.510
These two twin high school students
are my home tutors.

05:10.510 --> 05:14.280
Kai, the cool one, and Sei, the kind one!

05:14.280 --> 05:16.110
Good morning, Ichika.

05:16.110 --> 05:19.510
Kai and I will come over to
your house tomorrow.

05:19.510 --> 05:21.750
Yes, good morning!

05:21.750 --> 05:22.910
Um...

05:24.090 --> 05:27.680
Sei, thank you for this charm yesterday!

05:29.990 --> 05:30.960
It's okay.

05:31.930 --> 05:34.460
It was getting in the way and
I needed to get rid of it.

05:34.460 --> 05:38.470
Hey Sei! You didn't give Ichika
your trash, did you?

05:38.470 --> 05:40.370
It's not trash, really!

05:40.870 --> 05:42.170
I'll treasure it.

05:45.510 --> 05:47.270
Oh, no! We're going to be late!

05:48.280 --> 05:50.540
Go now. You'll be late.

05:50.550 --> 05:51.850
Until we meet again.

05:51.850 --> 05:52.810
Thank you!

05:54.620 --> 05:56.110
Goodbye!

06:10.100 --> 06:12.930
There aren't any classes on the final day
of the first term of school.

06:12.930 --> 06:15.640
The entire school is washed and swept clean,

06:15.640 --> 06:17.910
there's a closing ceremony,
and all we have is homeroom.

06:17.910 --> 06:21.070
If you don't clean properly,
I'll rewrite your report cards!

06:24.080 --> 06:26.350
The building we were in charge of cleaning

06:26.350 --> 06:29.480
is an old wooden school building
that isn't used anymore.

06:29.890 --> 06:33.340
So it's basically used for storage now, however...

06:34.160 --> 06:38.180
Hey, Keiko! stop that! The dust is...

06:39.230 --> 06:40.900
It's sparkling!

06:40.900 --> 06:44.170
Don't you think it's pretty, Satsuki?

06:44.170 --> 06:45.670
This is Keiko.

06:45.670 --> 06:49.870
She comes from a wealthy family and
is a kind and easygoing girl.

06:51.410 --> 06:54.240
It's not pretty! It's crap in the air!

06:54.240 --> 06:56.440
Particles! Dust! Filth!

06:56.440 --> 06:57.650
Sheesh!

06:57.650 --> 07:00.820
Satsuki is a very responsible
and dependable person.

07:00.820 --> 07:02.280
You can count on her!

07:02.600 --> 07:05.600
Oh? But it's so pretty... Isn't it nice?

07:05.600 --> 07:06.800
Michiru's really into literature,

07:06.800 --> 07:08.800
Michiru's really into literature,
No, it's not nice! It's dirt, and that's it!

07:09.100 --> 07:11.640
Michiru's really into literature,
and her instincts are amazingly sharp.

07:11.660 --> 07:12.760
Honestly, Satsuki...

07:12.760 --> 07:13.960
Honestly what?

07:13.960 --> 07:16.360
Come on everyone, let's clean!

07:25.410 --> 07:26.670
Ichika, you're such a stickler!

07:26.680 --> 07:27.870
Ichika, you're such a stickler!

07:28.180 --> 07:30.380
No, I'm not!

07:30.380 --> 07:32.010
Stickler!

07:32.010 --> 07:34.000
But, I'm not...

07:34.550 --> 07:37.040
"But I'm not!"

07:40.420 --> 07:44.760
Well, since Ichika asked us to,
let's finish up the cleaning quick.

07:44.760 --> 07:46.420
Roger!

07:59.770 --> 08:01.970
What's the matter? Did you see something?

08:02.480 --> 08:04.070
A woman...

08:11.220 --> 08:12.710
Now, now...

08:15.120 --> 08:16.450
Come on, we're getting on.

08:26.430 --> 08:30.300
The season of trials has come calling, yes?

08:40.880 --> 08:44.410
This mirror looks like it has quite a history...

08:45.890 --> 08:49.190
But it's been chipped. What a shame...

08:56.400 --> 08:57.460
Who was that?

09:00.940 --> 09:04.340
That was the girl that appeared in my dream.

09:05.710 --> 09:11.740
But at the time I couldn't remember the dream
for some reason.

09:13.550 --> 09:15.240
Speaking of which...

09:16.050 --> 09:17.120
What?

09:17.120 --> 09:21.620
That mirror you're dusting has
a scary legend about it, Ichika.

09:21.660 --> 09:24.290
What? It does?

09:24.290 --> 09:26.060
Oh, I know it!

09:26.060 --> 09:28.630
One of the seven mysteries, right Michiru?

09:28.630 --> 09:29.120
Yes.

09:32.330 --> 09:35.240
Michiru is one of those "with the vision".

09:35.240 --> 09:37.330
I cannot see that much, however.

09:38.440 --> 09:41.480
According to the legend,
when you stand in front of that mirror,

09:41.480 --> 09:44.640
you see the reflection of
a completely different person.

09:46.250 --> 09:49.980
Sheesh... You're such a scaredy-cat, Ichika.

09:49.980 --> 09:53.720
But... But! I just saw a strange girl in the mirror!

09:54.790 --> 09:56.550
Liar!

09:56.860 --> 10:00.800
N-no fair trying to scare us back!

10:00.800 --> 10:02.760
I'm not lying!

10:03.600 --> 10:05.360
For real?

10:06.230 --> 10:07.530
Hey!

10:08.400 --> 10:11.270
Come on now, are you done cleaning yet?

10:11.270 --> 10:12.870
It's already time for the closing ceremony.

10:13.310 --> 10:15.410
Oh, it's the teacher.

10:15.410 --> 10:17.180
Don't scare us like that.

10:17.180 --> 10:18.650
What do you mean "oh, it's the teacher"?

10:18.650 --> 10:20.750
Hurry up and go to the auditorium!

10:20.750 --> 10:21.210
Yes, Ma'am.

10:40.440 --> 10:44.100
The closing ceremony marks the end
of the first term of school.

10:44.770 --> 10:48.340
But for us, the real final rite of passage

10:48.340 --> 10:51.710
was getting our report cards instead of
listening to the Principal's speech.

10:58.290 --> 10:59.450
Now then...

11:01.860 --> 11:03.920
It's summer break!

11:04.860 --> 11:06.930
What are you going to do over summer break?

11:06.930 --> 11:09.730
Do you have plans to visit somewhere?

11:09.730 --> 11:13.730
My mom told me to study,
so we aren't vacationing anywhere.

11:13.940 --> 11:15.100
Listen up, folks!

11:15.100 --> 11:18.730
Entrance exams start in the summer of
your second year of middle school!

11:20.110 --> 11:21.280
Are you being serious?

11:21.280 --> 11:23.850
That's what the teach said, anyway...

11:23.850 --> 11:25.850
But hell if I wanna think about it.

11:25.850 --> 11:29.010
We will be third years next year, however.

11:29.380 --> 11:32.690
This really may be our final summer.

11:32.690 --> 11:36.180
Yeah. The final chance for us
to play around together.

11:37.590 --> 11:39.290
The... last?

11:39.660 --> 11:41.200
Let's have fun!

11:41.200 --> 11:44.000
Keep in touch every day, and just go wild!

11:44.530 --> 11:46.020
Roger!

11:46.330 --> 11:48.200
I won't accept any traitors!

11:51.770 --> 11:54.380
Okay, I'll contact everyone tomorrow!

11:54.380 --> 11:55.710
Roger!

11:56.840 --> 11:57.610
What's the matter?

11:58.410 --> 12:00.080
My cellphone...

12:00.080 --> 12:01.120
It's gone?

12:01.120 --> 12:02.840
It's not in your bag?

12:06.750 --> 12:07.990
No, it's not.

12:07.990 --> 12:10.730
Did you forget it at your house this morning?

12:10.730 --> 12:12.920
No, I'm sure I had it with me this morning.

12:16.460 --> 12:18.400
Maybe back then...

12:18.400 --> 12:19.420
Back then?

12:20.470 --> 12:23.840
It might have been when we were cleaning
in the old building...

12:26.040 --> 12:27.980
Um, would you guys...

12:27.980 --> 12:29.240
Sorry!

12:29.240 --> 12:32.910
My parents have been nagging me to hurry up
and show them my report card.

12:33.210 --> 12:35.850
I have a curfew...

12:35.850 --> 12:39.620
I am meeting with my mother after this.

12:41.060 --> 12:43.460
Just kidding! We'll go with you.

12:43.460 --> 12:44.220
Let's head back together.

12:45.230 --> 12:48.330
I'm okay! I can go by myself.

12:48.330 --> 12:51.600
I'm not that big of a scaredy-cat.

12:51.600 --> 12:53.030
In that case...

12:53.030 --> 12:53.600
Sorry!

12:53.600 --> 12:54.970
Sorry!

13:13.620 --> 13:18.150
I'm scared, but for the charm that Sei gave me...

13:25.770 --> 13:28.170
Is there anyone here?

13:28.170 --> 13:29.800
There isn't, is there?

13:30.200 --> 13:32.970
It's kind of scary, but...

13:39.980 --> 13:42.880
I think I dropped it around here...

13:44.450 --> 13:45.540
There it is!

13:50.260 --> 13:51.320
That's...

14:16.180 --> 14:18.450
Is this yours?

14:19.690 --> 14:21.160
Please, give it back!

14:21.160 --> 14:22.150
That's...

14:26.430 --> 14:29.120
This is yours, yes?

14:34.800 --> 14:36.830
That was the beginning.

14:37.140 --> 14:41.080
Our fateful encounter.

14:41.080 --> 14:43.340
And, parting...

14:46.150 --> 14:49.050
The trials begin.

14:51.550 --> 14:53.990
A favor?

14:54.460 --> 14:59.150
Yup! If you do a favor for me,
then I'll listen to your request.

15:00.930 --> 15:05.430
Don't worry! I won't tell you to
sell your soul or anything.

15:06.200 --> 15:07.630
Really?

15:07.640 --> 15:08.470
Yeah!

15:10.300 --> 15:12.930
The charm I received from Sei...

15:13.880 --> 15:15.140
What's the matter?

15:15.140 --> 15:17.180
Fine... then...

15:17.180 --> 15:18.650
Roger!

15:58.820 --> 16:02.520
This is... The color of the stones has changed!

16:02.520 --> 16:04.220
That won't do!

16:05.430 --> 16:06.990
Don't worry about that!

16:06.990 --> 16:07.760
See?

16:56.810 --> 16:57.780
My clothes!

16:58.280 --> 16:59.750
What is this?

17:00.050 --> 17:02.650
What is it? Um...

17:02.650 --> 17:05.720
It's like magic, right?

17:05.720 --> 17:07.490
Well, not exactly.

17:07.490 --> 17:09.290
But you can go ahead and think of it that way.

17:09.590 --> 17:12.080
But magic is...

17:15.700 --> 17:18.360
Who? Who are you?

17:36.250 --> 17:38.080
He is the Sun Djinn, Sola.

17:38.350 --> 17:42.850
You'd call him a god, or fairy, or spirit... I guess.

17:44.890 --> 17:48.400
Sola? The Sun fairy?

17:48.400 --> 17:50.500
Right! The Sun Djinn, Sola.

17:50.500 --> 17:55.000
By releasing the power of the Sola stone, you
have been blessed with the power of the sun.

17:55.700 --> 17:57.810
Those clothes are the proof of that.

17:57.810 --> 17:59.670
Power of the sun?

18:00.170 --> 18:02.510
I can't believe that!

18:02.510 --> 18:03.440
Really?

18:08.580 --> 18:10.050
This is...

18:47.250 --> 18:52.090
That was how I met a spirit of nature,
called a "Djinn".

18:52.460 --> 18:57.520
And I experienced their sense of perception.

18:59.000 --> 19:05.130
I wonder if the sun is always
watching over us all like this?

19:21.160 --> 19:22.320
How was it?

19:24.030 --> 19:26.360
Amazing, really amazing!

19:26.360 --> 19:30.060
Well, I'm glad! Here, write it down.

19:30.670 --> 19:33.470
Write it down? What do you mean?

19:33.470 --> 19:36.700
And this notebook is from a 100 yen store?

19:37.170 --> 19:39.140
You promised, right?

19:39.540 --> 19:46.340
I have to use 12 of those items this summer
and write down my impressions.

19:46.850 --> 19:49.850
Could you write them for me?

19:49.850 --> 19:54.350
This sounds a lot like you're trying to get me
to do your summer homework...

19:55.660 --> 19:58.890
I finally get to go on a
site-seeing trip to this world,

19:58.890 --> 20:02.060
so I don't wanna waste time
doing boring homework!

20:02.060 --> 20:04.260
That's irresponsible!

20:04.570 --> 20:06.000
Don't you worry 'bout that!

20:06.000 --> 20:08.940
I'll take responsibility, I promise.

20:08.940 --> 20:11.270
Here, let's pinky swear!

20:18.180 --> 20:18.700
And?

20:19.050 --> 20:22.020
She said she's Ichika's pen pal...

20:22.980 --> 20:24.750
I'm Manatsu Kuroki!

20:24.750 --> 20:26.620
Nice to meet you!

20:27.690 --> 20:30.490
It's just for summer break...

20:30.490 --> 20:32.320
She can't, right?

20:35.730 --> 20:38.070
She's a friend of yours, right Ichika?

20:38.070 --> 20:40.360
We'd be happy to have you stay in our home.

20:40.970 --> 20:42.830
Thanks a lot!

20:43.100 --> 20:45.170
Now, eat up!

20:45.170 --> 20:49.210
Ooh! Pressed sushi! I love that!

20:49.210 --> 20:51.080
It's nice when things are lively.

20:51.080 --> 20:53.050
Oh, can I watch television?

20:53.050 --> 20:54.050
Go ahead.

20:54.050 --> 20:57.180
The second episode of
"The Dune Bigshot" is on, right?

20:57.180 --> 20:59.720
Oh, so you're also a fan of Yamataku, Manatsu?

20:59.720 --> 21:00.740
So is Ichika.

21:02.390 --> 21:03.520
I prefer Makiko.

21:03.520 --> 21:06.630
Oh, you're so old fashioned, Ma'am!

21:06.630 --> 21:10.130
Oh, you're so old fashioned, Ma'am!

21:07.730 --> 21:10.390


21:21.410 --> 21:24.640
I'm sorry for lying to you.

21:32.820 --> 21:35.150
Now, show me...

21:36.590 --> 21:39.250
Show me your final choice...

21:47.500 --> 21:50.470


21:51.370 --> 22:00.930
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

21:51.370 --> 22:00.930
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

22:02.220 --> 22:13.720
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

22:02.220 --> 22:13.720
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

22:19.230 --> 22:29.000
Hora kotoshi mo ame furu gogo
hakanai utakata no iro

22:19.230 --> 22:29.000
See, this year the afternoon rain falls again
in the color of fleeting bubbles

22:30.080 --> 22:38.920
Sora mo yasashiku mienai wa
datte hitori da mono

22:30.080 --> 22:38.920
The sky doesn't look kind to me, after all,
I'm alone

22:40.550 --> 22:45.550
Itazura na sadame ni kotoba mo denai wa

22:40.550 --> 22:45.550
I have no more words for the tricks of fate

22:45.960 --> 22:53.360
Wakariaeta futari ni mou modorenai no?

22:45.960 --> 22:53.360
Can we never return to two
who understood each other?

22:53.930 --> 23:03.530
Ano hi deawanakereba ima mo
waraeteta no ka na?

22:53.930 --> 23:03.530
If we hadn't met that day,
would I have still been able to laugh now?

23:04.910 --> 23:16.610
Ano hi nakushita egao itsuka tokeru namida

23:04.910 --> 23:16.610
The smile I lost that day,
the tears that one day melt away...

23:20.460 --> 23:20.690


23:20.690 --> 23:22.030


23:22.030 --> 23:24.730
Until the moment when the two melt into one,

23:25.570 --> 23:31.570
The two of us clashed and struggled to the point
of frustration together.

23:31.940 --> 23:34.530
On that day I came to realize I enjoyed it.

23:35.080 --> 23:38.480
On the next Uta~Kata:
The Neighboring Night Sky
